      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are a few options for your policy introduction, depending on the tone you prefer. You could start by acknowledging the complex and evolving nature of this discourse, which is vital for good policy.\n\nFor one approach, you could state that the debate around the decolonization of collections involves strong arguments for the right of source communities to the return of their cultural heritage due to colonial history. However, others advocate for the continued role of major institutions in essential global research and the preservation of these unique objects in a secure, expert environment.\n\nThis framing allows you to state that the policy is designed to thoughtfully navigate these deeply held and often conflicting perspectives to determine the best way forward for the collection.",
